# Shipping Label format — APPROVED LOCK (2026-08-20)

The user approved the **current Shipping Label PDF layout** as the final format
as of this date. Do **not** "improve", tighten, or revert these values unless
the user **explicitly** asks to change the Shipping Label format.

## Locked SO / Contact spacing (`shipping_label_pdf.dart`)

| Constant / behavior | Approved value | Do not change to |
|---|---|---|
| `afterPillGap` (pill → SWIFT CONTACT label) | **11.0** | 6.0, 34.0, or other |
| Shipping under-pill `showRule` | **false** (default) | true on shipping |
| `contactLabelToValue` | **3.0** (same as `_fieldRow`) | 2.0 |
| Contact value box | **ink + 10, min 28**, **centered** via `_drawValue` | top-aligned compact `ink+6` |
| Contact field rule | **none** | hairline through name |
| Contact vs piece-band | name clears soft rule by **≥8pt** | overlap |

Receiving may still use `showRule: true` for SO→PM. That is separate from Shipping.
Receiving has its own improve loop: `qa_receiving/synthetic/` /
`scripts/receiving_label_improve_loop.py` / `.cursor/rules/receiving-label-improve-loop.mdc`.

## Locked customer logo sizing (red / green / pink) — updated 2026-09-05

Logos must **fill** their target height every time (scale up or down to match).
The only shrink exception is the pink limit (customer row would collide with Swift).

| Guide | Constant | PDF pt | px @ 72 dpi (1:1) | px @ 96 dpi | px @ 2× QA render |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Red** — square / circular (aspect **0.8–1.3**, see `LogoInkMetrics.isSquareOrCircle`) | `squareLogoTargetH` | **74.0** | **74** | **99** | **148** |
| **Green** — rectangular / tall / wide (aspect **&lt; 0.8 or &gt; 1.3**) | `rectLogoTargetH` | **58.0** | **58** | **77** | **116** |
| **Pink** — gap before Swift (never overlap) | `customerLogoToSwiftGap` | **12.0** | **12** | **16** | **24** |

Conversion: `px = pt × (dpi / 72)`. QA label previews use ~2 px per PDF pt.

Dual / mixed logos: each uses its own height class; if total ink width + gaps
would reach the pink edge, **uniform** height shrink. Never overlap the fixed
Swift logo.

**Red is intentionally taller than the Swift-fixed `customerLogoTargetH`
(62.24)** — a square/circular mark at Swift's height reads as smaller than a
wide rectangular one because it has far less ink width, so it washed out.
`_drawHeader`'s customer-logo band now grows **upward only** to fit
`squareLogoTargetH`, reaching into margin that was already empty above the
old band and stopping ~12pt clear of the real top bumper bar (`_bumper`) —
it never touches that bar and never moves `logoBottom` / the thin rule below
it (user-verified via the regression matrix: `pillToLabel`/`nameClear`/
Receiving `pill`/`rule` are byte-identical to pre-change values). Green
stays shorter than red on purpose — a wide mark at the red height would run
very wide and hit the pink limit sooner in dual-logo rows.

